                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af28a078-68c1-3e97-b44d-35e6c0e9de2a",
                        "entry_id": "774abb57-61ad-315d-b308-02d5397636f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To live under; live beneath (something); to fail to live up to (something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56211cd9-d02f-44bb-943c-3bd05d875f0c",
                                "sense_id": "af28a078-68c1-3e97-b44d-35e6c0e9de2a",
                                "text": "1684, Thomas Blomer (translator), “Coriolanus” in John Dryden (editor), Plutarch’s Lives, London: J. & R. Tonson and S. Draper, 1749, Volume 2, p. 244,\nSuch a Man looks upon Fame, not as a Reward of his present Virtue, but as an Earnest he has given of his future Performances; and is ashamed to underlive the Credit he has won, and not outshine his past illustrious Actions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddc47d4a-ba39-4061-a70b-beff871411c9",
                                "sense_id": "af28a078-68c1-3e97-b44d-35e6c0e9de2a",
                                "text": "They who are merely carried on by the wheel of such inclinations, without the hand and guidance of sovereign reason, are but the automatous part of mankind, rather lived than living, or at least underliving themselves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8535e88b-75b5-4027-ae58-5c987b800f4b",
                                "sense_id": "af28a078-68c1-3e97-b44d-35e6c0e9de2a",
                                "text": "1786, “A Set of Resolutions for Old Age” in Andrew Kippis (ed.), The New Annual Register, London: G.G.J. & J. Robinson, Volume 6, p. 233,\nNot to indulge too much in the luxury of the table, nor yet to underlive the constitution."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e5786e1-bdd0-42d7-8b59-0222459a210c",
                                "sense_id": "af28a078-68c1-3e97-b44d-35e6c0e9de2a",
                                "text": "We cannot afford to embark on a policy of paternalism in Latin America because of the damage it would do to us through underliving our basic ideals."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54a3a3f8-3a16-3aa2-a95c-c4d616390700",
                        "entry_id": "774abb57-61ad-315d-b308-02d5397636f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fail to reach (a certain age)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8ad11eb-c2ba-4ea2-8859-55b519a5e49c",
                                "sense_id": "54a3a3f8-3a16-3aa2-a95c-c4d616390700",
                                "text": "1901, Abstract of “The Duration of Life” by R. C. Brankston, The Charlotte Medical Journal, Volume 18, No. 5, May 1901, p. 425,\nIn the course of a few generations we shall have cultivated a vitality which would give us invariably at birth, an expectancy of 130 years, which age would be usual and except for unavoidable accident would never be underlived, but generally exceeded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "456cd5de-f9a9-4c2b-90fc-62ec9d82b7b1",
                                "sense_id": "54a3a3f8-3a16-3aa2-a95c-c4d616390700",
                                "text": "The duration of a person’s life is a mystery, and thousands of cancer patients have outlived or underlived their estimated life expectancy."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ff425ac-59fa-3e66-b4ab-d97f31cbd630",
                        "entry_id": "774abb57-61ad-315d-b308-02d5397636f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To live on fewer resources than (someone)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "479699e5-94dc-4c50-9f7b-287e8938a186",
                                "sense_id": "1ff425ac-59fa-3e66-b4ab-d97f31cbd630",
                                "text": "Many of that class who live in the country, and have farms, by their industry and frugal way of living, grow rich, for they can underlive the Britons, &c."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fc45636-1b04-460d-ab0c-9900d481271b",
                                "sense_id": "1ff425ac-59fa-3e66-b4ab-d97f31cbd630",
                                "text": "The Chinese go to stay. A few rebuffs do not dishearten them. Knowing their capacity to underlive and undersell their competitors, they are tenacious in the extreme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66a442c1-a943-42bc-a0b7-996f75313179",
                                "sense_id": "1ff425ac-59fa-3e66-b4ab-d97f31cbd630",
                                "text": "Fear of Japan, resulting from the contrast between the sparsely settled American and the thickly settled Asiatic shores of the Pacific Ocean and from the knowledge that the Asiatic exclusion policy has aroused great Japanese ill-feeling, and jealousy of Chinese and Japanese inhabitants of the U.S.A., resulting from their hard work, thrift, and skill, which enable them to underlive Americans of European origin, are political factors of importance in the Pacific region."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04132600-158d-4ba9-8682-3a896b4c4425",
                                "sense_id": "1ff425ac-59fa-3e66-b4ab-d97f31cbd630",
                                "text": "The family farmer, if he is not too deeply in debt, underlives the corporation farmer and survives."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12e0cf6b-6ab8-32b3-8fc5-531ca58a3dc7",
                        "entry_id": "774abb57-61ad-315d-b308-02d5397636f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To live on insufficient resources."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "089b12c1-4053-4bad-8b29-3f0f24005043",
                                "sense_id": "12e0cf6b-6ab8-32b3-8fc5-531ca58a3dc7",
                                "text": "Whole groups of underpaid workers may in consequence of underliving sink into such a condition of inefficiency and hopelessness that they are altogether powerless to extricate themselves from it by their own efforts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ace6c090-5583-475c-b3a0-a681737303c4",
                                "sense_id": "12e0cf6b-6ab8-32b3-8fc5-531ca58a3dc7",
                                "text": "It is stated that twenty-five full-time ministers received an average salary of $665.00, clearly an underliving wage."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "421f5389-4459-3617-a5ee-3773596a777f",
                        "entry_id": "774abb57-61ad-315d-b308-02d5397636f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To live in an overcautious or unfulfilling manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d37e2758-6bc8-46fb-9e2f-69a0bf9b5e7b",
                                "sense_id": "421f5389-4459-3617-a5ee-3773596a777f",
                                "text": "“Making plans based on professional advice can help you avoid overspending or underliving,” said Cottee. “An advisor will support you in making decisions based on fact, not fear, and ensure you have access to all the strategies you need to live an enjoyable and rewarding life in retirement.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
